    "body": "Related finding from the high-tier review of PR #1202 (2026-11-12, its review comment): `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps` posts an on-centre tap as a bare `G84 Z.. F..` under `G97 S.. M03`, with no rigid-tapping mode word (M29 on Fanuc-style controls). Many controls run a bare G84 as a floating-holder cycle; with a rigid holder that breaks the tap or strips the thread. It is main's existing output, unchanged by that PR. It belongs with this issue's rule: where the machine states rigid tapping, the lathe post writes the control's rigid-tap mode word; where it does not, the tap cycle is refused by name or posted with a note that a tension-compression holder is assumed.",
